{
  "body_human_readable": "### Oklahoma City Thunder Claims 2024-2025 NBA Championship Title\n\nThe Oklahoma City Thunder won the 2024-2025 NBA season, securing their first championship since relocating to the city. In a hard-fought series, the Thunder defeated the Eastern Conference champion Indiana Pacers in seven games. The championship is the franchise's second, with the first being in 1979 as the Seattle SuperSonics.\n\nThe Thunder's victory capped a dominant season where they finished with a league-best 68\u201314 regular-season record. The finals concluded on June 22, 2025, with Oklahoma City winning the decisive Game 7.\n\n**Key accolades for the season include:**\n*   **NBA Finals MVP:** Shai Gilgeous-Alexander was named the Finals MVP.\n*   **Most Valuable Player:** Shai Gilgeous-Alexander also earned the regular-season MVP award.\n*   **Rookie of the Year:** Stephon Castle was named the Rookie of the Year.\n\nThe series was the first NBA Finals to go to a Game 7 since 2016. The Thunder's victory also marked the NBA's seventh different champion in seven years, the longest such streak in league history.",
